From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: qcom: tsens: mask lower threshold interrupts across
 system suspend

The thermal core suspends all thermal zones at the start of
dpm_prepare(), before any device prepare callback runs. Suspending
from a warm state then guarantees that falling temperatures cross the
last-programmed lower trip thresholds, and the resulting level
interrupt can neither be serviced (zone updates are no-ops while
zones are suspended) nor cleared: it refires at handler-pass rate for
the rest of the transition and, being wake-armed, aborts every
suspend attempt at the noirq stage or wakes s2idle immediately.

Mask every sensor's lower threshold interrupt in a prepare callback,
which runs after the thermal core has quiesced zones (so nothing can
re-enable the interrupt) and before the suspend callbacks. Upper and
critical interrupts stay armed, so overheating during the transition
or during s2idle still wakes the system. No unmask is needed on
resume: the first post-resume update of each thermal zone re-enables
both directions via tsens_set_trips().

---
 drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
index 6e3714e..51f20ef 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens.c
@@ -1127,6 +1127,29 @@ static int tsens_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 	return priv->ops->get_temp(s, temp);
 }
 
+static int __maybe_unused tsens_prepare(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct tsens_priv *priv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	if (tsens_version(priv) < VER_0_1)
+		return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * The thermal core suspends every zone before device prepare
+	 * callbacks run, so a lower threshold crossed by falling
+	 * temperatures cannot be serviced and the level IRQ refires
+	 * until zones resume, aborting suspend once wake-armed.  Mask
+	 * LOWER across the transition; the first post-resume zone
+	 * update re-enables it through tsens_set_trips().  UPPER stays
+	 * armed so overheating still wakes the system.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < priv->num_sensors; i++)
+		tsens_set_interrupt(priv, priv->sensor[i].hw_id, LOWER, false);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int  __maybe_unused tsens_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
@@ -1155,7 +1178,10 @@ static int __maybe_unused tsens_resume(struct device *dev)
 	return tsens_resume_common(priv);
 }
 
-static SIMPLE_DEV_PM_OPS(tsens_pm_ops, tsens_suspend, tsens_resume);
+static const struct dev_pm_ops tsens_pm_ops = {
+	.prepare = pm_sleep_ptr(tsens_prepare),
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(tsens_suspend, tsens_resume)
+};
 
 static const struct of_device_id tsens_table[] = {
 	{
